  "notes": "Two sizes released together (8B and 32B), recorded as inline variants; they are built on different language models (see relations). Both use a SigLIP2-patch14-384 vision encoder, a third-party component that is not recorded as a relation. Announced by Cohere For AI, Cohere's research arm, since renamed Cohere Labs. The Aya 23 model cards call Aya Vision a multimodal variant in the Aya line, and the announcement says Aya Vision builds on Aya Expanse. The announcement says open weights for our 8b and 35b models in one place, an apparent slip for 32B. A technical report followed on arXiv in May 2025."
